  <link name="base_link">
    <!-- Chassis mass, weighed 2026-08-07.
       ========================================================
       The robot is 20 kg on a scale. This link carried 90.847,
       and the eight links together came to 94.280, which is 4.71 times
       the real machine. The exported inertia came out of CAD, so
       the likeliest cause is a material density that was never
       set; the shape is right and the density is not.

       Only this link is corrected. The other seven are left
       alone because their values are all plausible for the parts
       they describe: 0.566 kg for a 65 mm rubber drive wheel,
       0.115 kg for a caster wheel, 0.164 kg for the lidar
       (an RPLIDAR is about 0.19). Scaling those down with the
       chassis would have made them physically absurd to make an
       arithmetic total come out right.

       20 - 3.4325 (the other seven) = 16.5675, and the inertia
       scales with it at 0.182367 for unchanged geometry.

       What this changes, beyond the number:
         rotational inertia izz  4.167 -> 0.760 kg m^2
         drive wheel normal load  288 N -> 61 N
         caster scrub resistance 17.4 N -> 3.7 N

       And the centre of mass moves, because the wheels and
       casters (low and spread out) now carry a fifth of the
       robot instead of a twenty-fifth:
         x  +0.00087 -> -0.01089   (further behind the axle)
         z   0.22026 ->  0.20241   (lower)
       which takes the forward tipping deceleration from 6.82 to
       7.99 m/s^2. Correcting the mass made the robot harder to
       tip, not easier.

       [미검증] The distribution within this link is still CAD's.
       Weighing the drive and caster axles separately would give
       the real x, and a tilt test the real z; until then the two
       numbers above are the shape's, not the robot's. -->
    <inertial>
      <origin rpy="0 0 0" xyz="0.004031215194176557 3.002726997808124e-17 0.03506562657816282"/>
      <mass value="16.5675"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.438065" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.062604" iyy="0.660628" iyz="-0.0" izz="0.759891"/>
    </inertial>
